  "notes": "West leads the ♦Q against 6♥. East wins trick 1 with the ♦A and returns a diamond won by the ♦K. South draws trump, noting that West began with 2 hearts.\n\nSouth will have to perform some kind of squeeze. As West has shown the ♦J, a compound squeeze should be possible. South should run his trumps. On the second last trump West will be forced to abandon either spades or clubs. If South can read the position, a double squeeze will be established.\n\nIf West abandons spades, a spade is also thrown from dummy. The ♠K and ♠A are cashed next. The last trump will squeeze both defenders, West in diamonds and clubs and East in spades and clubs.\n\nOn the second last heart, if West had instead chosen to abandon clubs, a spade is thrown from dummy as before. The ♣K and ♣A are cashed next. On the last heart both defenders will be squeezed, West in diamonds and spades and East in clubs and spades.",
